{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a photoredox-catalyzed Nozaki-Hiyama reaction that is catalytic in chromium, utilizing air-stable Cr(III) salts instead of air-sensitive Cr(II). By employing a strong reducing TADF organic dye (5CzBn) and Hantzsch's ester as a sacrificial reductant under blue LED irradiation, the authors successfully generated nucleophilic organochromium(III) species from allyl halides for addition to aliphatic aldehydes. The study includes mechanistic photophysical investigations confirming a reductive quenching pathway.",
